@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+---
+id: task-001-give-tasks-stable-unique-identifiers
+type: task
+title: "Give tasks stable unique identifiers"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+Give every task a unique, stable string identifier when it is added. Expose lookup by identifier and
+let all title-oriented task operations accept either the current title or that identifier, so references
+remain valid after a rename.
+
+Acceptance criteria:
+
+- `add` returns a task with a unique string `id`.
+- `get(id)` returns the matching task using the same result convention as the existing list methods.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`, and `remove` resolve either a task title or
+  an identifier.
+- The public API documentation and tests cover the behavior.
